  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>Stop ten writes the terminal state. The record that was created as INIT is updated to Authorized or Declined, with the auth code and a processed timestamp. I want to highlight three things: this node is the single writer of the terminal transition, so the state machine is easy to read; it does not import anything from the bank package, so our domain model stays clean; and the authorization code is required only for Authorized, and that invariant is enforced by validation, not by hope.</p>
    </content>
